    "https://nec.peopleadmin.com/postings/6996": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Nursing Theory and/or Skills Lab",
      "description": "New England College Applicant Portal | Adjunct Faculty - Nursing Theory and/or Skills Lab Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Benefit Highlights Internal Recruitment Center To see available work study & graduate assistant jobs, use the “Current NEC Employees and Students Log In” then click “search student jobs” Adjunct Faculty - Nursing Theory and/or Skills Lab Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Adjunct Faculty - Nursing Theory and/or Skills Lab Position Purpose The adjunct nursing faculty supports New England College’s mission by delivering high-quality, evidence-based instruction to nursing students in theory and/or skills labs. This role aims to foster the development of competent, compassionate, and critical-thinking nurses prepared to meet the evolving demands of healthcare. Adjunct faculty contribute to student success by applying current nursing practice, engaging students through active learning strategies, and upholding the standards of professional nursing education and practice. Essential Duties Summary Deliver high-quality instruction by course objectives, whether in a classroom, laboratory, or simulation. Facilitate student learning using evidence-based, student-centered teaching strategies that reflect current nursing practice. Assess student learning through assignments, exams, and other evaluation tools; provide timely, constructive feedback. Maintain accurate records of student attendance and academic progress in accordance with program and college policies. Collaborate with full-time faculty and department leadership to ensure consistency in curriculum delivery and clinical expectations. Foster a professional and respectful learning environment that supports diverse learners and promotes equity and inclusion. Stay current with developments in the nursing profession and nursing education through ongoing professional development. Adhere to all regulatory, accreditation, and institutional standards, including those set by the New Hampshire Board of Nursing and CCNE . Required Qualifications Hold a current and active RN license in New Hampshire. A master’s degree in nursing. At least 2 years of relevant nursing experience in the specific area of educational responsibility, e.g., adult, pediatric, gynecologic/obstetric, or mental health. Experience educating nurses in practice and/or undergraduate pre-licensure academic settings. Preferred Qualifications EEO Statement New England College prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, creed or religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, age, marital status, pregnancy, veteran’s status or disability in regard to treatment, access to or employment in its programs and activities, in accordance with federal and state laws and regulations. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ), individuals with disabilities needing accommodation should contact the ADA Compliance Officer. Posting Detail Information Posting Number PT00125P Open Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Starting Salary $850 per credit Special Instructions to Applicants Reference Requests Reference Requests Minimum Requests Maximum Requests Cutoff Date Provider Special Instructions Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you live in CA, CO, or WA? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume/CV Optional Documents Cover Letter Henniker Campus 98 Bridge Street Henniker, NH 03242 603.428.2000 Contact Us: hr@nec.edu | 603-428-2359 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
