    "https://nec.peopleadmin.com/postings/6990": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Undergraduate Business, MBA, and DBA Programs",
      "description": "New England College Applicant Portal | Adjunct Faculty - Undergraduate Business, MBA, and DBA Programs Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Benefit Highlights Internal Recruitment Center To see available work study & graduate assistant jobs, use the “Current NEC Employees and Students Log In” then click “search student jobs” Adjunct Faculty - Undergraduate Business, MBA, and DBA Programs Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Adjunct Faculty - Undergraduate Business, MBA, and DBA Programs Position Purpose New England College seeks part-time undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral management faculty to develop and teach courses in a variety of disciplines: Accounting; Academic Writing; Organizational Behavior; Economics; Ethics; Finance; Entrepreneurship; Project Management; Strategic Research Project; Applied Statistics; Research Design; Advanced Research; Marketing; Data Visualization; Strategic Analysis; Management; Leadership; Operational Planning; Healthcare Management; Technology & AI Strategies. Management division undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral courses are offered on campus, online, and in hybrid and low-residency formats at the Henniker, NH campus. Faculty teaching in the Management graduate Spanish Language Programs must be bilingual (English and Spanish). Essential Duties Summary Develop and teach undergraduate business, MBA , and DBA courses. Review and grade work submitted by students and provide timely and substantive feedback. Coach struggling students towards course and program success. Teach the approved curriculum on the schedule to support student satisfaction. Engage students to facilitate and achieve course learning outcomes. Advise students on academics, attendance, and behavior expectations. Support retention by engaging students and contacting absent students to offer help. Advise students on research and consulting projects, internships, and practical training. Maintain and report student grades and attendance in accordance with institutional policy. Required Qualifications Excellent interpersonal, customer service, and presentation skills. Superior communication and problem-solving skills. Strong organizational skills; completes assignments accurately and on time. Proficiency with MS Office, Blackboard, and Canvas. Demonstrated ability to teach effectively at multiple college levels is essential. Earned master’s degree in business, research, or IT project management, plus either 18 graduate credits in the discipline or relevant professional certification and experience. Preferred Qualifications Earned doctoral degree in business, research, or IT project management, plus either 18 graduate credits in the discipline or relevant professional certification and experience. Record of intellectual and professional contributions in management or a related field, including publications and presentations. Experience serving on dissertation or strategic project committees. Independent research project mentoring is a plus. EEO Statement New England College prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, creed or religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, age, marital status, pregnancy, veteran’s status or disability in regard to treatment, access to or employment in its programs and activities, in accordance with federal and state laws and regulations. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ), individuals with disabilities needing accommodation should contact the ADA Compliance Officer. Posting Detail Information Posting Number PT00106P Open Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Starting Salary $667 Undergraduate online /$850 Undergraduate /$900 Graduate; per credit Special Instructions to Applicants Reference Requests Reference Requests Minimum Requests 3 Maximum Requests 3 Cutoff Date Provider Special Instructions Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you live in CA, CO, or WA? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Henniker Campus 98 Bridge Street Henniker, NH 03242 603.428.2000 Contact Us: hr@nec.edu | 603-428-2359 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://nec.peopleadmin.com/postings/6988": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Clinical Mental Health Counseling",
      "description": "New England College Applicant Portal | Adjunct Faculty - Clinical Mental Health Counseling Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Benefit Highlights Internal Recruitment Center To see available work study & graduate assistant jobs, use the “Current NEC Employees and Students Log In” then click “search student jobs” Adjunct Faculty - Clinical Mental Health Counseling Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Adjunct Faculty - Clinical Mental Health Counseling Position Purpose The adjunct faculty will provide remote asynchronous and synchronous instruction to master’s-level counseling trainees in courses such as Introduction to Counseling, Counseling Theories and Techniques, Professional Ethics, Skills in Helping Relationships, and others as they become available. Provide education through learning-centered instruction that will enable graduates to fulfill the evolving needs of the marketplace. Encourage a culture of learning that values mutual responsibility and respect, life-long learning, diversity and ethics as well as personal and professional development Essential Duties Summary • Perform faculty duties as outlined by the New England College Faculty Handbook; • Create a safe and supportive learning environment for students; • Provide course instruction as aligned with NEC Clinical Mental Health Counseling program expectations; • Manage the learning environment through keeping accurate records, submitting grades and other reports on time, and enforcing academic and attendance policies consistent with NEC ; • Report to Program Director. Required Qualifications • PhD in Counselor Education and Supervision (completed or in process), preferably from a CACREP -accredited program; • Previous experience in supervising master’s-level counseling trainees; • Experience with in-person, online, and hybrid teaching modalities; • Active clinical credentials; • Identified pedagogical style and record of strong teaching evaluations; • Dedication to social justice and equity for marginalized communities, especially CMHC students served by the program. Preferred Qualifications EEO Statement New England College prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, creed or religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, age, marital status, pregnancy, veteran’s status or disability in regard to treatment, access to or employment in its programs and activities, in accordance with federal and state laws and regulations. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ), individuals with disabilities needing accommodation should contact the ADA Compliance Officer. Posting Detail Information Posting Number PT00080P Open Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Starting Salary $1,400 per credit Special Instructions to Applicants Reference Requests Reference Requests Minimum Requests 0 Maximum Requests 3 Cutoff Date 06/30/2022 Provider Special Instructions Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you in the process of or have you already completed an Ed.D., Ph.D., or other relevant doctoral degree? Yes No If you have not yet completed an Ed.D., Ph.D., or other relevant doctoral degree, how far along are you in the process? (Open Ended Question) * Are you available to work in the evening (6 pm to 10 pm)? Yes No * Do you currently hold a NH License in the Mental Health field or are eligible for licensure? Yes No * Do you live in CA, CO, or WA? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Transcripts Letter of Recommendation Henniker Campus 98 Bridge Street Henniker, NH 03242 603.428.2000 Contact Us: hr@nec.edu | 603-428-2359 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    }
